**ANSWERS:**

> *The reasoning behind the answers is the following:*

> **2.2.1.** *The maximum of* $Z$ occurs when we win 100 times:
> $$\text{max}(Z) = 100(45) = 4500.$$

> **2.2.2.** *The minimum of* $Z$ occurs when we lose 100 times:
> $$\text{min}(Z) = 100(-5) = -500.$$

> **2.2.3.** *Since all* $X_i$s are iid, to obtain the expected value,
> we apply the following property: \begin{align*}
> \mathbb{E}(Z) &= \mathbb{E} \Bigg( \sum_{i=1}^{100} X_i \Bigg) \\
> &= \sum_{i=1}^{100} [\mathbb{E}(X_i)] \\
> &= 100 \mathbb{E}(X_i) \qquad \qquad \text{since they are identically distributed} \\
> &= 100(-3.6) = -360.
> \end{align*}

